5. Problem Solving:

**SOLVED (verified on hardware):** The SD "unrecoverable" failure. Root cause: the wedge was in the **controller**, not the card — its command state machine sticks in `CMD_BUSY` (`sr=0x00000001 why=noerr_but_cmd_busy`, no error bits), after which it silently refuses all commands (indistinguishable from a mute card). The fix is the official driver's `HAL_RCC_ResetModule(RCC_MOD_SDMMC1)` in `sd1_init()`, the single re-init entry point. **First `RECOVERED` ever observed** (build 202609161647): `CMD17 FAILED` → `re-identify (card mute…) mute_n=1` → `SD card init ok` → `re-identify OK (after 1 mute tries)` → `recovered after re-identify`, with a **full** recovery (eph inject 99 frames, both LFS healthy in `df`). Reproduced 4+ times across two logs. This also explains why 5 previous hard-reset attempts all failed (no module reset) and why only a board power cycle worked (a board reset resets this module too).

**Also solved:** device no longer dragged down by a dead card (BLE connects, GNSS stays `hz=1`, no IWDT reboot, `wait=0 ms` on hops) — the original "蓝牙异常" was `ble_companion` blocked on the dead SD (proven by a stall backtrace ending `sd1_send_cmd` ← `sf32lb_sd_cmd12`). DVFS governor stall reproduced at 142 s and was **auto-recovered by the new two-layer mechanism** (`diag: dvfs unhealthy` → `diag: dvfs restart` → `dvfs: gov re-armed by diag (recoveries=1)`), validating the user's long-standing "~2000 s DVFS stops" bug.

**Ruled out by measurement:** bad block (block 194 reads clean), DVFS as the cause of the *first* failure (3× proven — HCLK unchanged at the failure instant), writes/erases at boot (`hw_wr=0 erase=0`), PSRAM allocation (`eph-psram-done +1 ms`), mount quality (`try 1/3 ok in 48 ms`), and the SysTick timebase (`en=1 int=1 src=1`, `load` always = previous gear's HCLK/100 = constant 100 Hz, `val < load`).

**Still open:** (a) the **trigger** — why the controller enters `CMD_BUSY` at all; strongest remaining suspect is the 7 remaining `DCR = 0` sites in abort-and-retry paths (`sd1_wait_write`, `sf32lb_sd_read_block`, `sf32lb_sd_program_staged`, `sf32lb_sd_rt_xfer` ×3). The 17:07 build removed the `sd1_unstick_data` one and showed **zero `noerr_but_cmd_busy`** in that capture (sample of one). (b) The GNSS reader permanent stall (80 s, `reader not exited … skip join`), which the 200 ms clamp did **not** fix; recommended direction is a DWT cycle-counter-based non-blocking read loop + preallocated reader stack rotation (never `task_delete` a thread that may hold `g_sd_lock`). (c) Read-only consumer wiring (`sf32lb_sd_lfs_readonly()` has no callers). (d) `dynmodel bike failed (3/3)` (BIKE=10 never acks while AUTO=4 does). (e) `mmc5983 absent`, Umem SRAM 97%.

